Yices SMT Solver
=============================================

Copyright (c) 2026, SRI International
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

This applies to the Yices source. This archive also contains the GNU C
Library, GMP, and LibPoly. These are covered by the GNU Lesser General
Public License; NOTICES states which version applies to each. GMP and LibPoly
carry copyright notices in individual source files rather than one notice for
the project, so NOTICES reproduces no project-level copyright line for either.
For the GNU C Library, LICENSES/glibc-LICENSES.txt preserves the exact upstream
copying-permission notice collection. A relink kit for rebuilding against your
own versions of those libraries is published as a separate asset on the
release page.

Content
-------

This distribution includes four solvers

  bin/yices       (for the Yices 2 language)
  bin/yices-smt   (for SMT-LIB 1.2)
  bin/yices-smt2  (for SMT-LIB 2.0)
  bin/yices-sat   (sat solver, DIMACS format)

and the Yices library and header files

  lib/__DYLIB__
  lib/libyices.a
  lib/pkgconfig/yices.pc
  include/yices.h
  include/yices_types.h
  include/yices_limits.h
  include/yices_exit_codes.h


Examples and documentation are in the examples and doc directories.


The Yices shared library and the binaries other than the sat solver were
linked statically against GMP version __GMP__, copyright Free Software
Foundation (see NOTICES).


pkg-config
----------

The file lib/pkgconfig/yices.pc supports `pkg-config --cflags` and
`pkg-config --modversion` from the unpacked archive. The `--libs` and
`--static --libs` results do not produce a working link from the archive as
shipped. The archive has no unversioned shared-library link, so `-lyices`
selects libyices.a, and the private dependency archives named by Libs.private
are not included in lib/.

The installer creates the unversioned shared-library link and installs
yices.pc in <prefix>/lib/pkgconfig.


Shared-library runtime requirements
-----------------------------------

The four Linux executables are statically linked. The shared Yices library
is not: it loads libc.so.6, libm.so.6, libpthread.so.0, libstdc++.so.6, and
libgcc_s.so.1. A consumer needs compatible versions of those runtime
libraries. PROVENANCE identifies the producing toolchain; it is not a claim
that every distribution or runtime version has been tested. A kernel-version
minimum alone does not establish C++ runtime compatibility.

Before using the shared library on another system, inspect its dependencies
with ldd and compile and run a small client on that system. NOTICES explains
the mixture of static and dynamic runtime code in the library. RELINKING.md
and the separate relink kit describe rebuilding with a recipient's own
libraries and toolchain, whose runtime requirements may differ.


Installation
------------

The binaries can be used as is. To use the library, you'll need to
create symbolic links as follows:

  /sbin/ldconfig -n lib
  ln -sf __DYLIB__ lib/libyices.so

You can do the same thing with the shell script 'install-yices'
included in this distribution. Just type

  ./install-yices here



For a non-destructive installation, choose a fresh prefix that you own:

  YICES_PREFIX="$HOME/.local/yices-2.8.0"
  ./install-yices "$YICES_PREFIX"

This copies the binaries, headers, shared library, pkg-config file, and legal
record below that prefix. Add "$YICES_PREFIX/bin" to PATH when you want these
binaries. Library users can set PKG_CONFIG_PATH to
"$YICES_PREFIX/lib/pkgconfig".

The installer does not copy `lib/libyices.a` or `doc/manual.pdf`. Keep the
extracted distribution when you need the static archive or the manual.

The installer refuses to replace any existing Yices file or link. If you
intentionally want to replace an installation in a shared prefix, review that
prefix first and use the explicit option:

  sudo ./install-yices --replace-existing /usr/local





For more information about Yices, please visit https://yices.csl.sri.com.
